<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>First 90 Days in Spain: Complete Post-Arrival Checklist 2026 — Printable | My Spanish Visa</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    :root {
      --navy: #0c1930;
      --red: #be0011;
      --yellow: #facf39;
      --cream: #f8f7f4;
      --muted: #5a6478;
      --border: #dce3ed;
      --white: #ffffff;
      --green: #1b5e20;
      --green-light: #e8f5e9;
    }
    body { font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif; color: var(--navy); background: var(--white); line-height: 1.5; font-size: 13px; }

    .screen-header { background: var(--navy); color: var(--white); padding: 14px 24px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; }
    .screen-logo { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; }
    .screen-logo span { color: var(--yellow); }
    .print-btn { background: var(--yellow); color: var(--navy); border: none; padding: 9px 22px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; }
    .print-btn:hover { background: #e6bb2e; }

    .doc-header { background: var(--navy); color: var(--white); padding: 28px 36px 24px; }
    .doc-header-inner { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .doc-logo { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--yellow); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .doc-header h1 { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 6px; }
    .doc-header p { font-size: 0.82rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); }
    .doc-header-meta { display: flex; gap: 20px; margin-top: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .doc-meta-item { font-size: 0.78rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.65); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 2px; }

    .content { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 36px 40px; }

    .intro-box { background: var(--cream); border-left: 4px solid var(--yellow); padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px 0; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0; }
    .intro-box p { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }
    .intro-box strong { color: var(--navy); }

    /* WEEK SECTION */
    .week-section { margin: 28px 0; }
    .week-header { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0; }
    .week-header.week1 { background: var(--navy); color: var(--white); }
    .week-header.week2 { background: #1a3a5c; color: var(--white); }
    .week-header.month2 { background: #24426b; color: var(--white); }
    .week-header.month3 { background: #2d4a7a; color: var(--white); }
    .week-header.ongoing { background: var(--muted); color: var(--white); }
    .week-badge { background: var(--yellow); color: var(--navy); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 10px; white-space: nowrap; }
    .week-header h2 { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; }
    .week-header p { font-size: 0.75rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); margin-top: 2px; }
    .week-body { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-top: none; border-radius: 0 0 3px 3px; }

    /* TASK ITEM */
    .task-item { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 28px 1fr 70px 200px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); min-height: 42px; }
    .task-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
    .task-item.priority { background: #fffbec; }
    .task-cell { padding: 9px 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; }
    .task-cell.checkbox { justify-content: center; align-items: center; border-right: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .task-cell.label { border-right: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--navy); flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
    .task-desc { font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.4; }
    .task-cell.deadline-col { border-right: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.72rem; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; align-items: flex-start; gap: 2px; }
    .task-cell.notes { font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.4; }
    input[type="checkbox"] { width: 14px; height: 14px; cursor: pointer; accent-color: var(--navy); }

    .tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 2px; margin-top: 2px; }
    .tag-urgent { background: #f8d7da; color: var(--red); }
    .tag-important { background: #fff3cd; color: #856404; }
    .tag-legal { background: #d1ecf1; color: #0c5460; }
    .tag-dnv { background: #e0d7ff; color: #3a1e8c; }
    .tag-nlv { background: #d4edda; color: #155724; }
    .tag-all { background: #e2e3e5; color: #383d41; }

    .col-headers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 28px 1fr 70px 200px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: none; border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0; background: var(--cream); }
    .col-h { padding: 6px 10px; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--muted); }
    .col-h:first-child { border-right: 1px solid var(--border); text-align: center; }
    .col-h:nth-child(2) { border-right: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .col-h:nth-child(3) { border-right: 1px solid var(--border); }

    .tip-box { background: #fffbec; border: 1px solid #ffd166; border-radius: 4px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 12px 0; }
    .tip-box p { font-size: 0.8rem; color: #6b5000; line-height: 1.55; }
    .tip-box strong { color: #4a3800; }

    .warn-box { background: #fff5f5; border: 1px solid #ffb3b3; border-radius: 4px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 12px 0; }
    .warn-box p { font-size: 0.8rem; color: #8b0000; line-height: 1.55; }
    .warn-box strong { color: #5a0000; }

    /* QUICK REFERENCE */
    .quick-ref { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin: 20px 0; }
    .ref-card { background: var(--cream); border-radius: 4px; padding: 14px; border-top: 3px solid var(--navy); }
    .ref-card h3 { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .ref-card p { font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }
    .ref-card .phone { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-top: 6px; }

    /* CONTACTS TABLE */
    .contacts-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.78rem; margin-top: 8px; }
    .contacts-table th { background: var(--navy); color: var(--white); padding: 7px 10px; text-align: left; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; }
    .contacts-table td { padding: 7px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); }
    .contacts-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
    .contacts-table tr:nth-child(even) td { background: var(--cream); }
    .contacts-table td:first-child { font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); }

    .doc-footer { border-top: 2px solid var(--navy); padding: 16px 36px; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
    .doc-footer p { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--muted); }
    .doc-footer .logo-small { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); }

    @media print {
      .screen-header { display: none !important; }
      body { font-size: 11px; }
      .doc-header { padding: 20px 28px 16px; }
      .content { padding: 0 28px 24px; }
      .week-section { page-break-inside: avoid; }
      .quick-ref { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
    }
    @page { margin: 1.2cm; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="screen-header">
    <span class="screen-logo">My Spanish <span>Visa</span></span>
    <button class="print-btn" onclick="window.print()">⬇ Download / Print PDF</button>
  </div>

  <div class="doc-header">
    <div class="doc-header-inner">
      <p class="doc-logo">My Spanish Visa · myspanishvisa.com</p>
      <h1>First 90 Days in Spain: The Complete Post-Arrival Checklist</h1>
      <p>TIE card, NIE, padrón, bank account, health insurance, utilities — everything new Spain residents need to do</p>
      <div class="doc-header-meta">
        <span class="doc-meta-item">Updated: April 2026</span>
        <span class="doc-meta-item">Week-by-week format</span>
        <span class="doc-meta-item">Covers NLV, DNV and Student Visa holders</span>
        <span class="doc-meta-item">Includes Beckham Law deadline reminder</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content">

    <div class="intro-box">
      <p><strong>Important:</strong> Some post-arrival tasks have strict legal deadlines. <strong>TIE card applications must be made within 30 days of arrival.</strong> For DNV holders, the Beckham Law application window opens from your first social security registration — you have 6 months. Tasks marked <span class="tag tag-urgent">URGENT</span> have fixed deadlines. Tasks marked <span class="tag tag-dnv">DNV</span> or <span class="tag tag-nlv">NLV</span> apply to specific visa holders. All others apply to everyone.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- WEEK 1 -->
    <div class="week-section">
      <div class="week-header week1">
        <span class="week-badge">WEEK 1 · Days 1–7</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Immediate Priorities</h2>
          <p>Complete these as soon as possible after arriving — some can be done on your first day</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-headers">
        <div class="col-h">✓</div>
        <div class="col-h">Task</div>
        <div class="col-h">Priority</div>
        <div class="col-h">Notes / How to Do It</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-body">
        <div class="task-item priority">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Register padrón (empadronamiento) at your local Ayuntamiento (town hall)
            <span class="task-desc">The municipal census registration. Required before your TIE appointment.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-urgent">URGENT</span><span style="font-size:0.7rem; color: var(--muted);">Before TIE appt.</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Bring: passport, rental contract / property deed. Collect the padrón certificate (volante de empadronamiento) — you will need it for your TIE appointment. Some councils allow online registration; most require in person.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item priority">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Book your TIE card appointment (cita previa)
            <span class="task-desc">Book at extranjeria.ses.mir.es or icp.administracionelectronica.gob.es. Appointments fill up fast.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-urgent">URGENT</span><span style="font-size:0.7rem; color: var(--muted);">Apply within 30 days</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Book your appointment immediately — slots are often 2–4 weeks out. Select "Solicitud de autorización de residencia" or the relevant TIE option for your visa type.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Purchase a local SIM card or activate roaming plan
            <span class="task-desc">You'll need a working Spanish phone number for online bookings and verification codes.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-all">ALL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Major providers: Movistar, Vodafone, Orange. Budget options: Pepephone, Lebara, Digi. SIM is available from any phone shop or supermarket. You can upgrade to a contract once you have NIE/TIE.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Open a Spanish bank account (or begin application)
            <span class="task-desc">Needed for rent payments, utilities, salary, and direct debits. Some banks can open accounts without TIE.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-important">IMPORTANT</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Expat-friendly banks: BBVA, Sabadell, CaixaBank, Openbank (online). Bring: passport, NIE/TIE (or apply as non-resident initially), padrón certificate, proof of income. Some banks require TIE — open a non-resident account first if needed.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Confirm your rental or property address is correct on all documents
            <span class="task-desc">Ensure your accommodation address matches your padrón and will match your TIE.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-all">ALL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Any inconsistency between your address on documents can delay TIE processing. If subletting, ensure landlord will provide a support letter if needed.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Verify your health insurance is active and covers your Spanish address
            <span class="task-desc">Ensure your Spanish health insurance policy is active from arrival date.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-all">ALL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Contact your insurer to confirm policy is active and note the emergency contact number. Save the number in your phone immediately.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="warn-box"><p><strong>TIE deadline:</strong> You must apply for your TIE card within <strong>30 days of entering Spain on your visa</strong>. Failure to apply in time can complicate your residency status and may result in a fine. Book your cita previa on your first or second day in Spain — appointments are typically 1–3 weeks away.</p></div>

    <!-- WEEKS 2-4 -->
    <div class="week-section">
      <div class="week-header week2">
        <span class="week-badge">WEEKS 2–4 · Days 8–30</span>
        <div>
          <h2>TIE Card and Admin Setup</h2>
          <p>Attend TIE appointment, complete NIE registration, and get essentials in place</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-headers">
        <div class="col-h">✓</div>
        <div class="col-h">Task</div>
        <div class="col-h">Priority</div>
        <div class="col-h">Notes / How to Do It</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-body">
        <div class="task-item priority">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Attend TIE appointment at Oficina de Extranjería
            <span class="task-desc">Submit TIE application and documents.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-urgent">URGENT</span><span style="font-size:0.7rem; color: var(--muted);">Within 30 days</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Bring: original passport + copy, visa entry stamp, padrón certificate, 2 biometric photos, completed EX-17 form, Modelo 790 Code 12 fee receipt (approx. €15 — pay at bank). Keep the appointment receipt — needed to collect TIE.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Collect your TIE card (separate appointment)
            <span class="task-desc">TIE collection requires a second visit, typically 30–60 days after application.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-important">IMPORTANT</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">You will be notified when your TIE is ready. Bring your original application receipt and passport to collect. Your TIE is your official Spain residency card — carry it at all times.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Confirm your NIE number
            <span class="task-desc">Your NIE (Número de Identidad de Extranjero) is your Spanish tax and ID number. It's printed on your TIE.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-all">ALL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Your NIE is used for all financial and legal dealings in Spain — bank accounts, property purchases, tax returns. Note it down and keep it secure.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Set up utilities — electricity (luz), water (agua), and internet
            <span class="task-desc">Transfer existing contracts into your name or set up new ones.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-all">ALL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Electricity: Endesa, Iberdrola, or smaller suppliers. Internet: Movistar, Vodafone, Orange. You will need your NIE, padrón, and bank account details to set up direct debits. Internet installation can take 1–2 weeks.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Register with a local GP (médico de cabecera)
            <span class="task-desc">Register with your health insurer's GP network or nearest primary care clinic.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-all">ALL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Take TIE, padrón certificate, and health insurance card to your nearest clinic (centro de salud). Ask your insurer for the nearest in-network doctors.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Notify your home country tax authority of your move (if required)
            <span class="task-desc">Some countries require notification when you establish tax residency abroad.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-important">IMPORTANT</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">UK: HMRC P85 form. US: Report to IRS annually (FBAR/FATCA). Canada: T1 emigrant return. Australia: ATO notification. Consult a cross-border tax advisor if in doubt.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MONTH 2 -->
    <div class="week-section">
      <div class="week-header month2">
        <span class="week-badge">MONTH 2 · Days 31–60</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Settling In and Admin Completion</h2>
          <p>Sort your phone contract, schools, and set up financial admin properly</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-headers">
        <div class="col-h">✓</div>
        <div class="col-h">Task</div>
        <div class="col-h">Priority</div>
        <div class="col-h">Notes / How to Do It</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-body">
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Set up a Spanish mobile phone contract (with TIE/NIE)
            <span class="task-desc">Upgrade from prepay SIM to a monthly contract with data.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-all">ALL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Now you have your TIE/NIE you can sign a proper contract. Compare at comparatel.es. You'll need: TIE/NIE, passport, bank account details for direct debit.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Register children for school (if applicable)
            <span class="task-desc">State schools (colegios públicos) are free. Private and international schools have fees.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-all">ALL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Contact your local Consejería de Educación or Ayuntamiento for state school placement. Bring: TIE/passport, padrón, child's birth certificate, immunisation records, previous school reports. Spanish language support (apoyo lingüístico) is usually available.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Set up Spanish bank direct debits for utilities, rent, and insurance
            <span class="task-desc">Ensure all recurring payments are linked to your Spanish bank account.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-all">ALL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Automated direct debits (domiciliación) are standard practice in Spain for all bills. Contact each provider with your new Spanish IBAN to set these up.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Register with Spanish Social Security (Seguridad Social)
            <span class="task-desc">Required for DNV holders and anyone working in Spain.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-dnv">DNV</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Visit your nearest Tesorería General de la Seguridad Social office. Bring TIE, passport, and employment/autónomo documentation. Your social security number (número de afiliación) triggers the Beckham Law application deadline.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Register as autónomo if self-employed (DNV holders working freelance)
            <span class="task-desc">Self-employed workers must formally register with Hacienda and Seguridad Social.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-dnv">DNV</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">File Modelo 036/037 (tax registration) and Alta en Autónomos (social security). Monthly autónomo fee approx. €230–400 depending on income. Consider a gestoria to handle this. Do this before issuing invoices to clients.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Open additional savings account or investment account if needed
            <span class="task-desc">Separate accounts for different purposes help with Spanish tax reporting.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-important">IMPORTANT</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Keep foreign income and Spanish income accounts clearly separated. This simplifies annual tax return preparation significantly.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MONTH 3 -->
    <div class="week-section">
      <div class="week-header month3">
        <span class="week-badge">MONTH 3 · Days 61–90</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Digital Certificate, Driving Licence, and Tax Registration</h2>
          <p>Complete your digital identity setup and critical government registrations</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-headers">
        <div class="col-h">✓</div>
        <div class="col-h">Task</div>
        <div class="col-h">Priority</div>
        <div class="col-h">Notes / How to Do It</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-body">
        <div class="task-item priority">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Obtain digital certificate (certificado digital) via FNMT
            <span class="task-desc">Electronic identity for online dealings with all Spanish government agencies.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-important">IMPORTANT</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Apply online at sede.fnmt.gob.es → "Certificado de Persona Física". Enter your NIE, complete online verification, then attend an FNMT registration office in person to confirm identity (bring TIE + passport). Download certificate to your computer once confirmed. Essential for Hacienda, Seguridad Social, and Extranjería dealings online.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item priority">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Apply for Beckham Law (Régimen Especial de Impatriados) — DNV holders
            <span class="task-desc">File Modelo 149 with Agencia Tributaria to elect the special tax regime.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-dnv">DNV</span><span class="tag tag-urgent">6 MONTHS</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">CRITICAL: You have 6 months from your first social security registration to apply. Use your digital certificate to file Modelo 149 via the Agencia Tributaria (AEAT) website, or engage an asesor fiscal (tax advisor) to file on your behalf. Missing this window permanently forfeits the benefit.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Begin driving licence exchange process (if required)
            <span class="task-desc">Non-EU driving licences must be exchanged for a Spanish licence within 6 months (for countries with reciprocal agreements) or earlier.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-legal">LEGAL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">UK licence holders must exchange within 6 months of becoming resident. US and Australian licences must usually be exchanged or a Spanish test taken. Visit your local DGT (Dirección General de Tráfico) office. Book via sede.dgt.gob.es. Bring TIE, current driving licence, photos, and fee payment.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Register as a taxpayer with Agencia Tributaria (Hacienda)
            <span class="task-desc">Register for Spanish income tax if not already done through autónomo registration.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-important">IMPORTANT</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">If you become tax resident in Spain (183+ days), you must file an annual tax return (declaración de la renta) for the year. Spanish tax year is the calendar year. First return is filed April–June of the following year. Use your digital certificate to access Hacienda online.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Register car or motorbike in Spain (if you brought a vehicle from abroad)
            <span class="task-desc">Foreign-registered vehicles must be re-registered in Spain if you are a resident.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-legal">LEGAL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">You have 6 months from residency to register a foreign vehicle. Contact DGT and an ITV (vehicle inspection) station. Bring: purchase invoice, current registration certificate, TIE, insurance. Import duty may apply.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="task-item">
          <div class="task-cell checkbox"><input type="checkbox"></div>
          <div class="task-cell label">
            Notify padrón of any address changes
            <span class="task-desc">If you move address, update your padrón immediately — it affects your TIE renewal address.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cell deadline-col"><span class="tag tag-all">ALL</span></div>
          <div class="task-cell notes">Visit your new Ayuntamiento with new rental contract/property deed and passport/TIE. Get a new padrón certificate showing your current address.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box"><p><strong>Digital certificate tip:</strong> Install your certificado digital in multiple browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari) as soon as you download it. Also export a backup copy and store it securely. Without it, you must visit government offices in person for everything — with it, you can handle 95% of bureaucracy from home.</p></div>

    <!-- ONGOING -->
    <div class="week-section">
      <div class="week-header ongoing">
        <span class="week-badge">ONGOING</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Ongoing and Annual Tasks</h2>
          <p>Regular tasks to maintain your legal residency status in Spain</p>
        </div>
